Hi there,

I am working with `counterfact@2.9.0` and I am encountering an issue where the OpenAPI spec declares a query parameter that is of type object.
Take following spec:

```json
{
  "openapi": "3.1.2",
  "info": {
    "title": "Test API",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "paths": {
    "/test": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getTest",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "pageable",
            "in": "query",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Pageable"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": {
    "schemas": {
      "Pageable": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "page": {
            "type": "integer",
            "format": "int32",
            "minimum": 0
          },
          "size": {
            "type": "integer",
            "format": "int32",
            "minimum": 1
          },
          "sort": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

At `types/paths/test.types.ts` we get following type for the query parameters:
```ts
export type getTest_Query = { pageable: Pageable };
```
with: (`types/components/schemas/Pageable.ts`)
```ts
export type Pageable = {
  /**
   * @format int32
   */
  page?: number;
  /**
   * @format int32
   */
  size?: number;
  sort?: Array<string>;
};
```

According to the OpenAPI definition (v3.x), query params of type object should be exploded by default (for `in` = `query`, the default of `style` is `form` - and `style` = `form` makes `explode` default to `true`, [see here](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/main/versions/3.1.2.md#fixed-fields-for-use-with-schema)).
So this endpoint should be called like this: `http://localhost:3100/test?page=0&size=100&sort=a&sort=b&sort=c`

However, if you try to call it like this, you get following response:

> Request validation failed:
> query parameter 'pageable' is required

The request validation is wrong here - no `pageable` query parameter should be expected. Instead it should be looked for `page`, `size` or `sort` parameters (none of them is required by the `Pageable` schema, but as the `pageable` parameter is required, at least one of its properties should be sent).

I have no clear opinion if the parameters should live at `$.query.pageable` or directly at `$.query` (which would also require to change the types mentioned above). I guess one can make arguments for both - it would just be great if the validation is corrected and the parameters are accessible via one way or the other.

Setting `"style": "form", "explode": true` additionally manually for the parameter also does not change the behavior - it is still ignored.

Thanks :)

PS: Swagger sadly also does not explode query params, so SwaggerEditor also does not handle this properly.

The spec property of the config file can be an array of objects with the following keys:

- source: path to OpenAPI file 
- prefix: URL prefix
- group: name of a subdirectory where the code is output

Runner will have a computed property named subdirectory that is either "" or "/${this.group}" 

So that we don't have branches for single vs. multiple specs everywhere, normalize the config by wrapping a single spec in an array. 

app.js will map the array to an array of ApiRunners. 

group will be passed as an optional second argument to ApiRunner.create() (default value = "") and exposed as a public readonly property. 

createKoaApp() will accept an array of runners and loop over them. 

```ts 
for (runner of runners) { 
  app.use(
    openapiMiddleware("/counterfact/openapi${runner.subdirectory}", {
      path: runner.openApiPath,
      baseUrl: `//localhost:${config.port}${runner.prefix}`,
    }),
  );

  app.use(
    koaSwagger({
      routePrefix: "/counterfact/swagger${runner.subdirectory}",

      swaggerOptions: {
        url: "/counterfact/openapi${runner.subdirectory}",
      },
    }),
  );

  if (config.startAdminApi) {
    app.use(
      adminApiMiddleware(
        "/_counterfact/api${runner.subdirectory}",
        runner.registry,
        runner.contextRegistry,
        config,
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

The base property will be added to the basePath for CodeGenerator.

    this.codeGenerator = new CodeGenerator(
      this.openApiPath,
      config.basePath + this.subdirectory,
      config.generate,
    );

For now the REPL will be configured using the first item in the array.

